hadiths[54]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1527","[AI-translation] Juhani from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad! Command your companions to raise their voices with the Talbiyah, for it is among the rituals of Hajj."
"1528","[AI-translation] On the authority of Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet: Perform Hajj and Umrah frequently, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows removes impurities from iron."
"1529","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him): The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said while he was in Makkah and intending to depart—and Umm Salamah had not performed Tawaf of the House and wanted to depart—so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to her: ""When the Fajr prayer is established, perform Tawaf on your camel while the people are praying."" So she did that, and she did not pray until she departed."
"1530","[AI-translation] From Umm Salamah, she said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I did not perform the Tawaf of departure."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""When the prayer is established, perform Tawaf on your camel from behind the people."
"1531","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When you throw the Jamarat, it will be light for you on the Day of Judgment."
"1532","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When you have thrown the Jamrah, everything becomes permissible for you except women."
"1533","[AI-translation] On the authority of Aishah, raised to the Prophet: When one of you completes his Hajj, let him hasten his journey to his family, for it is greater in reward."
"1534","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from her father, that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said to him: ""Let your sister Aishah ride behind you and take her for Umrah from at-Tan'im. When you descend the hill, instruct her to enter Ihram, for it is an accepted Umrah."
"1535","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas: The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: ""Hasten from Batn Muhassir, and use pebbles the size of Khadhf pebbles."
"1536","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas: Quraysh said, ""Muhammad and his companions have been weakened by the fever of Yathrib."" So when the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) arrived in the year he performed Umrah, he said to his companions: ""Perform Ramal around the House, so that the polytheists may see your strength."" When they performed Ramal, Quraysh said, ""They have not been weakened."
"1537","[AI-translation] He (peace be upon him) said: ""Throw the Jamrah with pebbles like those of Khadhf."
"1538","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet: ""Enjoy this House, for it has been destroyed twice, and it will be raised in the third."
"1539","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""O Allah, this is a Hajj in which there is no ostentation and no seeking of fame."
"1540","[AI-translation] It was narrated from 'Aishah that she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, entered upon me when four or five nights of Dhu al-Hijjah had passed during his Hajj, and he was angry. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, may Allah cast into the Fire whoever made you angry?!"" He said: ""Do you not know that I commanded them with a matter and they are hesitating? Had I known beforehand what I learned afterward, I would not have driven the sacrificial animal nor bought it until I exited Ihram as they exited."
"1541","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""Indeed, Allah says: 'A servant whose body I have made healthy and whose livelihood I have expanded, and five years pass over him without him coming to visit Me, is deprived.'"
"1542","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet, peace be upon him, when he threw the Jamarat, would walk to them both going and returning."
"1543","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The days of Tashriq are days of eating and remembrance."
"1544","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Jabir, raised to the Prophet: ""The piety of Hajj is feeding food and good speech."
"1545","[AI-translation] He, peace be upon him, said: ""Perform Hajj and Umrah in succession, for they remove poverty and sins just as the bellows remove the impurities of iron."
"1546","[AI-translation] It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The menstruating woman and the postpartum woman, when the time arrives, should perform ritual bathing, enter Ihram, and perform all the rituals except Tawaf of the House."
"1547","[AI-translation] Siddiq that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was asked: ""What is the best of Hajj?"" He said: ""Loudly proclaiming the Talbiyah and spilling blood."
"1548","[AI-translation] Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The pilgrims and the performers of Umrah are the delegates of Allah; He called them and they answered Him, they asked Him and He gave them."
"1549","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn Umar, raised to the Prophet: There are five animals for which there is no sin upon the Muhrim in killing them: the crow, the kite, the mouse, the scorpion, and the vicious dog."
"1550","[AI-translation] Narrated from Ibn Abbas, raised to the Prophet: The best water on the face of the earth is the water of Zamzam; in it is nourishment for the hungry and a healing from illness. And the worst water on the face of the earth is the water of Wadi Barahut, the remnant of Hadramawt, like the leg of a locust among the creeping things; it flows in the morning and by evening it has no moisture."
"1551","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The shepherd throws at night, and grazes during the day."
"1552","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The shepherd throws at night, and grazes during the day."
"1553","[AI-translation] From Aishah that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said to her: Your Tawaf of the House and between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah is sufficient for your Hajj and your Umrah."
"1554","[AI-translation] Al-Fadl bin Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to the people when they departed on the eve of Arafah and the morning of Jam: Adhere to tranquility. And he was restraining his she-camel until, when he entered Mina, he descended when he descended at Muhassir, and said: Take the pebbles for throwing with which the Jamarah is pelted."
"1555","[AI-translation] Narrated from Bahz bin Hakim from his father from his grandfather (Muawiyah bin Haidah), who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The cutter of the Sidr tree, Allah casts his head into the Fire."
"1556","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas said: He, peace be upon him and his family, when he pelted Jamarat Al-Aqabah, would depart and not stop."
"1557","[AI-translation] From Ibn Umar: He, peace be upon him and his family, when he performed Tawaf of the House, would wipe, or he said: touch, the Stone and the Corner in every Tawaf."
"1558","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Umar: He (peace be upon him) used to, when it was a day before Tarwiyah, address the people and inform them of their rituals."
"1559","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurayrah: It was among his Talbiyah (peace be upon him): ""Here I am, O God of Truth."
"1560","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah: She used to carry some Zamzam water and would report that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to carry Zamzam water (in vessels and waterskins), and he would pour it over the sick and give it to them to drink."
"1561","[AI-translation] Narrated Uthman bin Affan: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to cover his face while he was in Ihram."
"1562","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to visit the House every night of the nights of Mina."
"1563","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas: He (peace be upon him and his family) used to visit the House every night of the nights of Mina."
"1564","[AI-translation] All the days of Tashriq are for slaughter."
"1565","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""All the mountain passes of Makkah are a route and a place of slaughter."
"1566","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir who said: We used to take the meat of the sacrificial animals as provisions to Madinah during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family)."
"1567","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah: A scorpion stung the Prophet (peace be upon him) while he was praying, so he said: ""May Allah curse the scorpion, it spares neither a praying person nor anyone else, so kill it in the Hill and the Haram."
"1568","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas, as marfu: There is no shaving for women; rather, upon women is only shortening (of the hair)."
"1569","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, as marfu: No one pronouncing the Talbiyah has ever done so except that he was given glad tidings, and no one proclaiming the Takbir has ever done so except that he was given glad tidings. It was said: With Paradise? He said: Yes."
"1570","[AI-translation] From Aishah that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: There is no day on which Allah frees a servant from the Fire more than the Day of Arafah. And He draws near, then boasts about them to the angels and says: What do these desire?"
"1571","[AI-translation] Juhani who said: My sister vowed to walk to the Ka'bah barefoot and bareheaded. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, came to her and said: What is the matter with her? They said: She vowed to walk to the Ka'bah barefoot and bareheaded! He said: Command her to ride, let her wear a Khimar, let her perform Hajj, and let her offer a sacrificial animal."
"1572","[AI-translation] Khattab who said: It is from the Sunnah to alight at Al-Abtah on the eve of Nafr."
"1573","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: Whoever circumambulates the House seven times and prays two Rakahs, it is as if he freed a slave."
"1574","[AI-translation] From Abdullah bin Hubshi who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Whoever cuts down a Sidr tree, Allah will cast his head into the Fire (meaning from the Sidr trees of the Haram)."
"1575","[AI-translation] From Ibn Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: No woman should perform Hajj except with a Mahram. A man said: O Prophet of Allah! I have been enlisted for such-and-such campaign, and my wife is going for Hajj. He said: Go back and perform Hajj with her."
"1576","[AI-translation] Aslami: That he saw a man on a camel following the people's tents at Mina, with the Prophet of Allah, peace be upon him, present, and the man was saying: Do not fast on these days, for they are days of eating and drinking. Qatadah said: It was mentioned to us that that caller was Bilal."
"1577","[AI-translation] From Umm Walad Shaybah who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, performing Sa'y between As-Safa and Al-Marwah, and he was saying: The valley is not to be traversed except briskly."
"1578","[AI-translation] Jawni that he performed Hajj with his mawali. He said: I went to Umm Salama and said: O Mother of the Believers! I have never performed Hajj, so with which of the two should I begin, Hajj or Umrah? She said: If you wish, perform Umrah before you perform Hajj, and if you wish, after you perform Hajj. I went to Safiyya and she said to me the like of that. I returned to Umm Salama and informed her of the statement of Safiyya. Umm Salama said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, say: O family of Muhammad! Whoever of you performs Hajj, let him enter the state of ihram for an Umrah during his Hajj."
"1579","[AI-translation] From Bilal bin Rabah that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said to him on the morning of Jam': O Bilal, quiet the people, or silence the people. Then he said: Verily Allah has shown grace to you in this gathering of yours, and He has gifted your wrongdoers to your righteous ones, and has given your righteous ones what they asked for. Depart in the name of Allah."
"1580","On the authority of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), attributed to the Prophet (ﷺ): ""O ʿĀʾishah! Were it not that your people are recent converts from polytheism (and I do not have sufficient means to rebuild it), I would have spent the treasure of the Kaʿbah in the cause of Allah, and I would have demolished the Kaʿbah and leveled it to the ground, then rebuilt it upon the foundations of Ibrāhīm, and I would have made for it two doors set at ground level—an eastern door through which people would enter, and a western door through which they would exit—and I would have added six cubits to it from the Ḥijr."" In a narration: ""And I would have included the Ḥijr within it, for Quraysh had shortened it when they built the Kaʿbah. If your people should decide to rebuild it after me, come, let me show you what they left out of it."" So he showed her approximately seven cubits. In a narration from her: She said, ""I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the Jidar (the wall)—meaning the Ḥijr—'Is it part of the House?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'Then why did they not include it in the House?' He said: 'Your people ran short of funds.' I said: 'What is the matter with its door being raised high?' He said: 'Your people did that so they could admit whom they wished and prevent whom they wished.'"" In a narration: ""...out of arrogance, so that none would enter it except whom they wished. Thus, when a man wished to enter it, they would let him climb up until, when he was about to enter, they would push him, so he would fall. Were it not that your people are recent converts from the Jāhiliyyah, and I fear their hearts would deny [the change], I would have included the Jidar in the House and set its door at ground level."" (So when Ibn al-Zubayr gained authority, he demolished it and made for it two doors.) In a narration: ""That is what prompted Ibn al-Zubayr to demolish it."" Yazīd ibn Rūmān said: ""I witnessed Ibn al-Zubayr when he demolished it and rebuilt it, and he included the Ḥijr within it. I saw the foundations of Ibrāhīm (peace be upon him); they were stones interlocked like the humps of camels, tightly interlocked."""
